&Q000557 = Letter from Išbi-Erra to Ibbi-Suen about the purchase of grain
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.1.17
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.1.17&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. {d}i-bi₂-{d}suen lugal-ŋu₁₀-ra u₃-na-a-dug₄
#lem: Ibbisuen[1]RN; lugal[king]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: Say to @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}}, my lord: this is what @wRN{Išbi-@wDN{Erra}}, your servant, says: 
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. {m}iš-bi-er₃-ra arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: Išbierra[1]RN; arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. kaskal i₃-si-in{ki} ka-zal-lu{ki}-še₃
#lem: kaskal[way]; Isin[1]SN; Kazallu[1]SN
#tr.en: You ordered me to travel to @wSN{Isin} and @wSN{Kazallu} to purchase grain. 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. še sa₁₀-sa₁₀-de₃ (1:a₂-še₃ mu-e-da-a-aŋ₂:1)
#lem: še[barley]; sa[pay for]; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: With grain reaching the exchange rate  
#etcsl: line-id=4

:4v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) im-kur₉#-re#-en#
#lem: kur[enter]

5. ganba 1 še gur-ta-am₃ še sa₂ di
#lem: šakanka[market price]; n; še[barley]; gur[unit of capacity]; še[barley]; sa[equal]; di[speak]
#tr.en: of one shekel of silver per @fsux{gur}, 
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. 20 gun₂ kug-babbar še (1:sa₁₀-sa₁₀-de₃:1) ba-an-ŋar
#lem: n; gun[load]; kugbabbar[silver]; še[barley]; sa[pay for]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: 20 talents of silver have been invested for @varh[t3117.v1]{the purchase } @vart[t3117.v2,t3117.v1]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} …… } of grain. 
#etcsl: line-id=6

:6v.1.1: ($2 mss. have instead:$) SAM₂-re-de₃
#lem: X

7. inim mar-tu lu₂-kur₂-ra šag₄ ma-da-zu kur₉-ra ŋiš bi₂-tuku
#lem: inim[word]; Martu[1 Amorite]; lukur[stranger]; šag[heart]; mada[land]; kur[enter]; ŋeš[tree]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: I heard news that the hostile @wEN{Martu} have entered inside your territories. 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. 72000 še gur še du₃-[a]-bi# šag₄# i₃-si-in{ki#}-na-ke₄ (1:ba-an-kur₉-re-en:1)
#lem: n; še[barley]; gur[unit of capacity]; še[barley]; du[all]; šag[heart]; Isin[1]SN; kur[enter]
#tr.en: @varh[t3117.v3]{I entered with 72,000 @fsux{gur} of grain } @vart[t3117.v4,t3117.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} 72,000 @fsux{gur} of grain was brought } -- the entire amount of grain -- inside @wSN{Isin}. 
#etcsl: line-id=8

:8v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) ba-an-kur₉{+ur#}
#lem: kur[enter]

9. a-da-al-la-bi mar-tu du₃-du₃-a-bi šag₄ kalam-ma-še₃ ba-an-kur₉-re-en
#lem: adallabi[now]; Martu[1 Amorite]; du[all]; šag[heart]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: Now I have let the @wEN{Martu}, all of them, penetrate inside the Land, 
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. bad₃ gal-gal dili-dili-bi im-mi-in-dab₅-dab₅
#lem: bad[wall]; gal[big]; dili[single]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: and one by one I have seized all the fortifications therein. Because of the @wEN{Martu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. mu mar-tu še-ba sag₃-ge (1:nu-mu-e-da-šum₂-mu:1)
#lem: mu[name]; Martu[1 Amorite]; še[barley]; sag[strike]; šum[give]
#tr.en: @varh[t3117.v5]{I am unable to hand over } @vart[t3117.v6,t3117.v5]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} I am unable to make …… } this grain for threshing. They are stronger than me, 
#etcsl: line-id=11

:11v.1.1: ($2 mss. have instead:$) [...]-mu-un-da-ak-e
#lem: ak[do]

12. ugu-ŋu₁₀ mu-ta-ni-kalag i₃-tuš-u₃-de₃-en
#lem: ugu[skull]; kalag[strong]; tuš[sit (down)]
#tr.en: while I am condemned to sitting around. 
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. lugal-ŋu₁₀ 600 (1:{ŋiš}ma₂-gur₈:1) 120 gur-ta-am₃ he₂-em-du₈-e
#lem: lugal[king]; n; magur[barge]; n; gur[unit of capacity]; du[spread]
#tr.en: Let my lord repair 600 @varh[t3117.v7]{barges } @vart[t3117.v8,t3117.v7]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} boats } of 120 @fsux{gur} draught each; 
#etcsl: line-id=13

:13v.1.1: ($2 mss. have instead:$) ma₂
#lem: ma[ship]

14. {ŋiš}ma₂ 72 kalag-ga 20 {ŋiš}ZA PI# X# 30 X X GAN
#lem: ma[ship]; n; kalag[strong]; n; ZA[type of boat]; X; X; n; X; X; X
#tr.en: 72 solid boats, 20 ……, 30 ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. 50 {ŋiš}X 60 {ŋiš}ig ma₂# ugu# ma₂# ŋa₂-ŋa₂#
#lem: n; X; n; ig[door]; ma[ship]; ugu[skull]; ma[ship]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: placing (?) 50 …… and 60 (?) boat doors on the boats (?), 
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. u₃ {ŋiš}ma₂ du₃-a-bi he₂-X
#lem: u[and]; ma[ship]; du[all]; X
#tr.en: may he also …… all the boats. 
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. id₂-da {id₂}kur-ra {id₂}pa-li-iš-tum-ta
#lem: id[river]; Idkura[1]WN; Palištum[1]WN
#tr.en: @varh[t3117.v9]{Let them bring it up } @vart[t3117.v10,t3117.v9]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} May he make them go out } by water, along the @wWN{Kura} and the @wWN{Palištum} watercourses, 
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. du₆ sal-la-še₃# (1:he₂-em-ta-ed₃-de₃-eš!:1)
#lem: dud[(ruin) mound]; sal[thin]; ed[go up]
#tr.en: to the grain heaps (?) that are spread out. And I myself intend to @varh[t3117.v11]{go (?) } @vart[t3117.v12,t3117.v11]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} come out } and meet them (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=18

:18v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) [...]-bi₂#-ib-ed₂-de₃#
#lem: e[leave]

19. u₃ ŋe₂₆-e igi-ni-še₃ (1:ga-am₃-ma-ši-ŋen:1)
#lem: u[and]; ŋaʾe[I]; igi[eye]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: The place there where the boats moor will be under my responsibility. 
#etcsl: line-id=19

:19v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) ga-am₃-ta#-e₃#
#lem: e[leave]

20. ki {ŋiš}ma₂ kar-bi ugu-ŋa₂ e-tuku
#lem: ki[place]; ma[ship]; kar[harbor]; ugu[skull]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: Let them load up huge amounts of grain (?), 
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. HI-HI še du₃-a-bi he₂-ŋa₂-ŋa₂ he₂-e-sa₂#
#lem: X; še[barley]; du[all]; ŋar[put]; sa[equal]
#tr.en: the entire amount of grain; it should reach (?) you. 
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. tukum-bi še ba-an-tur-re-en
#lem: tukumbi[if]; še[barley]; tur[small]
#tr.en: If you have not got enough grain, 
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. ŋe₂₆-e še ga-mu-ra-kur₉
#lem: ŋaʾe[I]; še[barley]; kur[enter]
#tr.en: I myself shall have grain brought in to you. 
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. lugal-ŋu₁₀ elam-ma{ki} šen-šen-na zi ba-an-ir
#lem: lugal[king]; Elam[1]GN; šen[battle]; zi[life]; ir[cvve]
#tr.en: My lord has become distressed about the battles in @wGN{Elam}. 
#etcsl: line-id=24

25. še-ba-ni ul₄-la-bi al-til-la
#lem: še[barley]; ul[hasten]; til[complete]
#tr.en: But the @wEN{Elamites'} grain rations have quickly been exhausted, 
#etcsl: line-id=25

26. lirum-lirum na-an-tah-en
#lem: lirum[strength]; tah[add]
#tr.en: so do not slacken your forces! 
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. nam-arad-da-ni-še₃ saŋ-zu na-an-šum₂-mu-un
#lem: namarad[slavery]; saŋ[head]; šum[give]
#tr.en: Do not fall head first into their slavery, 
#etcsl: line-id=27

28. u₃ egir-ra-ni-še₃ na-an-du-un
#lem: u[and]; egir[back]; du[go]
#tr.en: nor follow at their heels! 
#etcsl: line-id=28

29. še mu 15-ta-am₃ šag₄-gal e₂-gal-zu
#lem: še[barley]; mu[year]; n; šaggal[food]; egal[palace]
#tr.en: I have at my disposal enough grain to meet the needs  
#etcsl: line-id=29

30. u₃ iri (1:du₃-a-bi:1) šu-ŋu₁₀-ta i₃-ŋal₂
#lem: u[and]; iri[city]; du[all]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: of your palace and of @varh[t3117.v13]{all the cities } @vart[t3117.v14,t3117.v13]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} all your cities } for 15 years. 
#etcsl: line-id=30

:30v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) du₃-a-zu
#lem: du[all]

31. (1::1) i₃-si-in{ki} nibru{ki}-a (2:en-nu-uŋ₃ ha-ra-ab-ak-e:2)
#lem: Isin[1]SN; Nibru[1]SN; ennuŋ[watch]; ak[do]
#tr.en: @varh[t3117.v15]{That I should guard for you } @vart[t3117.v16,t3117.v15]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} To guard } @vart[t3117.v17,t3117.v17]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} the city of } @wSN{Isin}, 
#etcsl: line-id=31

:31v.1.1: ($1 ms. adds:$) iri
#lem: iri[city]
:31v.2.1: ($2 mss. have instead:$) en-nu-uŋ₃ ak-de₃
#lem: ennuŋ[watch]; ak[do]

32. (1:ugu-ŋa₂ he₂-tuku:1)
#lem: ugu[skull]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: and @wSN{Nibru}: @varh[t3117.v18]{let it be my responsibility. 
#etcsl: line-id=32

:32v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) lugal-ŋu₁₀ ugu-ŋa₂ e-tuku
#lem: lugal[king]; ugu[skull]; tuku[acquire]

33. lugal-ŋu₁₀ he₂#-en-zu
#lem: lugal[king]; zu[know]
#tr.en: } @vart[t3117.v19,t3117.v18]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} my lord, is this my responsibility? } My lord should know this! @noteref{end of shorter version} 
#etcsl: line-id=33

$ (end of shorter version)
34. lugal-ŋu₁₀ ni₂ nu-te ni₂ nu-gid₂-i šag₄-ba ŋe₂₆-e nu-te#-BU
#lem: lugal[king]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]; ni[self]; gid[long]; šag[heart]; ŋaʾe[I]; X
#tr.en: My lord, I am without fear! I will not delay (?); I will not …… in their midst. 
#etcsl: line-id=34

35. diŋir dili-dili-bi igi he₂-ni-ib₂-kiŋ₂-kiŋ₂-e ki-bi he₂-kiŋ₂-kiŋ₂#
#lem: diŋir[deity]; dili[single]; igi[eye]; kiŋ[seek]; ki[place]; kiŋ[seek]
#tr.en: Each one of @wSN{Isin's} and @wSN{Nibru's} gods may search there for faces (?); I have indeed looked for them. 
#etcsl: line-id=35

36. uŋ₃ daŋal-bi nam-lu₂-ulu₃-bi!# [...] X BI mah
#lem: uŋ[people]; daŋal[wide]; namlulu[humanity]; X; X; X; mah[great]
#tr.en: Their widespread people, their population ……, huge ……, are indeed healthy; 
#etcsl: line-id=36

37. he₂-silim-me-eš# numun zid-da (1:he₂-en-gal-le#-eš:1)
#lem: silim[healthy]; numun[seed]; zid[right]; gal[big]
#tr.en: the true seed is @varh[t3117.v20]{indeed great there } @vart[t3117.v21,t3117.v20]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} precious }. 
#etcsl: line-id=37

:37v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) [...]-kal#-le-eš
#lem: kal[rare]

38. urim₂{ki} iri# kug-zu an ki-da# mu₂#-a
#lem: Urim[1]SN; iri[city]; kug[pure]; an[sky]; ki[place]; mu[grow]
#tr.en: @wSN{Urim}, your holy city, rivalling heaven and earth, whose great prince you are ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=38

39. nun gal-me-e GAG X X saŋ-ki-bi kal-la
#lem: nun[prince]; gal[big]; X; X; X; saŋki[forehead]; kal[rare]
#tr.en: of which the appearance is precious, 
#etcsl: line-id=39

40. me šum₂-mu uš ŋiš-hur# ge#-en-gen₆-ne₂ sig igi-nim-ma
#lem: me[Being]; šum[give]; uš[foundation]; ŋešhur[plan]; gin[confirm]; sig[weak]; iginim[upper land]
#tr.en: which dispenses the divine powers and makes the foundations (?) and the plans firm both in the south and in the uplands, 
#etcsl: line-id=40

41. šu-ta he₂-kar-re KA# X X-bi he₂-eb₂-be₂
#lem: šu[hand]; kar[flee]; X; X; X; e[speak]
#tr.en: will surely escape from the grasp and will cry ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=41

42. e₂-kiš-nu-ŋal₂ eš₃ an ki šu₂-šu₂ X X X nu-tuku
#lem: Ekišnuŋal[1]TN; eš[shrine]; an[sky]; ki[place]; šuš[cover]; X; X; X; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: @wGN{Elam}, a raging dog, a destroyer, will not defile @wTN{E-kiš-nu-ŋal}, 
#etcsl: line-id=42

43. elam{ki} ur-idim lu₂ niŋ₂ ha-lam-ma-ke₄
#lem: Elam[1]GN; uridim[mad dog]; lu[person]; niŋ[thing]; halam[forsake]
#tr.en: the sanctuary which covers heaven and earth, which has no ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=43

44. šu pe!-el nu-ma-ak-e {d}lamma-bi nu-si-il#
#lem: šu[hand]; pel[defile]; ak[do]; lammar[(female) tutelary deity]; sil[split]
#tr.en: Its protective spirits shall not be split apart! My lord: 
#etcsl: line-id=44

45. lugal-ŋu₁₀ KA sig₁₀-sig₁₀ gal-gal dub₃-tuku mu-un#-kar#
#lem: lugal[king]; X; sig[put into]; gal[big]; dubtuku[runner]; kar[flee]
#tr.en: the loudest roarer (?), the runner, has taken flight (?)! 
#etcsl: line-id=45

46. {m}i-bi-{d}suen-ka šag₄-ta-am₃ ki aŋ₂#-me-eš
#lem: Ibbisuen[1]RN; šag[heart]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: May @wDN{An}, @wDN{Enlil} and @wDN{Enki}, who have loved @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}} from the womb, look upon him approvingly. 
#etcsl: line-id=46

47. an {d}en-lil₂ {d}en!-ki igi zid hu-mu-un-ši-bar-re-e-ne
#lem: An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; Enkik[1]DN; igi[eye]; zid[right]; bar[place outside]
#tr.en: …… is indeed placed there; 
#etcsl: line-id=47

48. [X X] X X RU E X X X he₂-en-ŋar igi-bi he₂-eb₂-[gi₄]-gi₄
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; X; X; X; X; ŋar[put]; igi[eye]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: they have changed (?) their appearance. 
#etcsl: line-id=48

49. X X abula! urim₂{ki}-ma ŋal₂ da₁₃!-da₁₃!-da a-a
#lem: X; X; abula[gate]; Urim[1]SN; ŋal[open]; taka[set aside]; aya[father]
#tr.en: With the …… and (?) the city-gates of @wSN{Urim} opening, they cry @q{“Aee!”} 
#etcsl: line-id=49

50. X he₂-ni!-ib-be₂ a-ba-am₃ lugal-ŋu₁₀-e-še
#lem: X; e[speak]; aba[who?]; lugal[king]
#tr.en: If …… says, @q{“Who is my lord?”} 
#etcsl: line-id=50

51. lugal# {d}en-lil₂# X X gaba-ri nu-tuku-me-en#
#lem: lugal[king]; Enlil[1]DN; X; X; gabari[equal]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: -- You are the king to whom @wDN{Enlil} has given …… no rival! 
#etcsl: line-id=51

52. [...] X X X [...] šag₄-zu na-an-gig-ga#
#lem: X; X; X; X; X; šag[heart]; gig[sick]
#tr.en: Your heart should not fret over this, ……! 
#etcsl: line-id=52

53. [...] šu mu-un#-gi suhuš-bi mu-ri-in-ge-en
#lem: X; šu[hand]; gi[turn]; suhuš[foundation]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: For …… has avenged (?) ……; he has made its foundations firm for you. 
#etcsl: line-id=53

54. [...] X numun-bi-a šag₄-zu he₂-en-dug₃-ge
#lem: X; X; numun[seed]; šag[heart]; dug[good]
#tr.en: Let your heart be glad over …… and (?) its seed. 
#etcsl: line-id=54

55. en#-na lugal-ŋu₁₀ al-til₃-la nam-lugal urim₂{ki} mu-un-ak-e
#lem: enna[until]; lugal[king]; til[live (of a single person)]; namlugal[kingship]; Urim[1]SN; ak[do]
#tr.en: As long as my lord is alive, he will exercise kingship over @wSN{Urim}. 
#etcsl: line-id=55

56. niŋ₂ na-me lugal-ŋu₁₀ kiŋ₂ mu-na-ni-ib₂-gi₄
#lem: niŋ[thing]; name[any]; lugal[king]; kiŋ[work]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: Do not suddenly reject anything that is sent as a message (?) to my lord! 
#etcsl: line-id=56

57. a-ma-ru-kam nam-ba-e-šub-de₃-en-ze₂-en
#lem: amaru[flood]; šub[fall]
#tr.en: Before @wDN{Utu}, 
#etcsl: line-id=57

58. igi# {d}utu-kam ka-ŋu₁₀ nu-bala-e
#lem: igi[eye]; Utu[1]DN; kag[mouth]; bala[turn]
#tr.en: I will not change my word (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=58







